  "worked_solution": "The position of the particle at $t=2$ is equal to its position at $t=0.5$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0.5,2].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(2)=x(0.5)+{\\int }_{0.5}^{2}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) & ={e}^{2}+{\\int }_{0.5}^{2}{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+{[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t+1}]}_{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(2)+1}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(0.5)+1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{5}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=2$ is $x=\\frac{{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}}{2}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
